WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:05.904
(intense music buildup)

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:08.220
- It's keto time!

00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:13.317
(techno intro music)

00:00:13.317 --> 00:00:15.017
Keto, Keto, Keto. I challenged you

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:18.340
to get my keto video to
twenty thousand likes

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.560
and you surpassed that goal plenty.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.760
And I'm actually really
excited about this.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.120
I'm unfortunately fresh out of a break up

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.860
so I'm more motivated than ever

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.450
to change my lifestyle
around, be healthier,

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.030
look better, I wanna take you guys

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.000
along for that journey.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.070
My one month of keto starts now.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.653
(intense orchestral music)

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:52.893
- Just do it!

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:59.533
All right, I'm gonna have
my very first keto meal.

00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:01.503
It's the middle of the day,
I didn't have breakfast

00:01:01.503 --> 00:01:02.853
so I guess you could say I'm

00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:04.793
intermittent fasting today as well.

00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:09.793
This is my meal here, beef
chili with oaxaca cheese?

00:01:10.543 --> 00:01:12.873
Oaxaca? And cauliflower rice.

00:01:12.873 --> 00:01:15.503
To my surprise, the first few days of keto

00:01:15.503 --> 00:01:18.423
weren't that bad. I was
totally expecting that

00:01:18.423 --> 00:01:21.493
I would go with keto flu
symptoms right off the bat.

00:01:21.493 --> 00:01:24.043
It wasn't that bad, I didn't
have sugar withdrawal.

00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:45.623
The weight stayed the same,
my strength was there,

00:01:45.623 --> 00:01:48.043
but I'd fatigue much earlier in my sets.

00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:51.093
Can't even be certain it's
to do with the keto diet,

00:01:51.093 --> 00:01:52.926
but that's what was happening.

00:01:57.905 --> 00:01:59.933
All right, my man just shot a shot,

00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:01.633
made me drop my phone.

00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:03.413
This guy right here, wanna
be basketball player.

00:02:03.413 --> 00:02:05.563
All right, today's my first day of cardio

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.103
with keto on board and I gotta admit,

00:02:09.103 --> 00:02:10.436
I'm feeling pretty tired.

00:02:11.343 --> 00:02:12.743
I just beat both of these guys though.

00:02:12.743 --> 00:02:15.323
I was able to keep up with
them, my sprints were fine,

00:02:15.323 --> 00:02:18.793
my game was fine, but I noticed
that after a game or two,

00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:20.533
when I would be somewhat out of breath,

00:02:20.533 --> 00:02:23.215
I was totally burnt. I was really tired,

00:02:23.215 --> 00:02:24.953
much more than usual.

00:02:24.953 --> 00:02:27.111
Again, not certain that it's 100 percent

00:02:27.111 --> 00:02:28.963
due to the keto diet,
but I do suspect keto

00:02:28.963 --> 00:02:32.256
is playing a role in my
decreased stamina in my exercise.

00:02:34.177 --> 00:02:36.746
The keto struggle is so real,

00:02:37.804 --> 00:02:38.637
I'm eating cat food.

00:02:38.637 --> 00:02:40.473
- Let me at least fix my
hair a make sure I look good.

00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:44.723
- While Lisa's eating a healthy
salad with some croutons.

00:02:44.723 --> 00:02:47.003
- I'm eating cat food.

00:02:47.003 --> 00:02:48.933
Tell them about the cat food.

00:02:48.933 --> 00:02:49.853
- [Lisa] It's salmon!

00:02:49.853 --> 00:02:50.686
- What damn cat food?

00:02:50.686 --> 00:02:52.473
- He's eating cat food, it's right there.

00:02:52.473 --> 00:02:54.283
- That's called the keto struggle.

00:02:54.283 --> 00:02:57.343
Going into the second week of keto,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.148
I was starting to struggle a lot

00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:00.933
with my food choices.

00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:04.283
When I go to work, and I'm
gonna be working a long shift,

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.831
I can't bring all of
these goodies, an avocado,

00:03:06.831 --> 00:03:08.053
and all this stuff.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.523
So, what did I do?

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:12.643
I brought a Thrive Market can of salmon,

00:03:12.643 --> 00:03:15.613
with some mayonnaise and
I basically ate cat food.

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:18.213
Eating a diet that's so high in fat,

00:03:18.213 --> 00:03:20.723
I mean 75 percent of
my calories were coming

00:03:20.723 --> 00:03:23.333
from fat, it's difficult

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:25.463
to maintain that and I don't plan well.

00:03:25.463 --> 00:03:27.713
For example, if I'm going to a big event,

00:03:27.713 --> 00:03:29.626
I should probably eat beforehand.

00:03:41.593 --> 00:03:44.383
You have to plan ahead if
you wanna stick to keto.

00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:46.363
Because when you go to a fast food joint,

00:03:46.363 --> 00:03:49.433
or a restaurant, yes they
may have a piece of meat,

00:03:49.433 --> 00:03:51.543
but eating high protein is not keto.

00:03:51.543 --> 00:03:53.183
You have to be eating high fat.

00:03:53.183 --> 00:03:54.693
So you have to be thinking about what

00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:56.323
it is you're gonna choose off the menu.

00:03:56.323 --> 00:03:58.931
And you can get a cheeseburger
that's very fatty,

00:03:58.931 --> 00:04:01.646
has sauce on it that's
hopefully carb free,

00:04:01.646 --> 00:04:04.549
that's not optimal keto.
That's the dirty keto

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:05.973
that people talk about.

00:04:05.973 --> 00:04:08.843
If you're eating high saturated
fats, over cooked red meats,

00:04:08.843 --> 00:04:11.383
using processed oils, that's
not something I generally

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.036
recommend or want for myself.

00:04:15.057 --> 00:04:15.890
Wait!

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.873
(police sirens)

00:04:17.873 --> 00:04:21.213
Two weeks in, I already
had some results showing.

00:04:21.213 --> 00:04:23.323
My clothes were fitting
better, my abs were

00:04:23.323 --> 00:04:25.213
coming out of hibernation,
like one of them

00:04:25.213 --> 00:04:27.173
legit came out and said, "What up!"

00:04:27.173 --> 00:04:29.003
And I was like, "Oh my god look its my ab,

00:04:29.003 --> 00:04:30.513
I used to see you back in the day

00:04:30.513 --> 00:04:31.663
and then you started hibernating."

00:04:31.663 --> 00:04:32.629
It did surprise me that after two weeks

00:04:32.629 --> 00:04:35.323
of keto, I was already
starting to see results

00:04:35.323 --> 00:04:37.464
and now I get why this diet is so popular

00:04:37.464 --> 00:04:40.273
amongst people who are trying
to lose weight quickly.

00:04:40.273 --> 00:04:42.203
And not that I'm advocating for that,

00:04:42.203 --> 00:04:44.412
but it was nice to see
results so early on,

00:04:44.412 --> 00:04:46.113
and quite motivational.

00:04:46.113 --> 00:04:48.523
I will say though, the
majority of the weight loss

00:04:48.523 --> 00:04:49.643
that happens in the first week

00:04:49.643 --> 00:04:51.243
or so is usually water weight.

00:04:51.243 --> 00:04:54.616
That's not gonna be sustainable,
that speed of weight loss.

00:04:56.323 --> 00:04:59.993
I feel like on keto, I
wake up really hungry.

00:04:59.993 --> 00:05:02.423
Normally I don't mind skipping breakfast,

00:05:02.423 --> 00:05:04.503
but on keto I'm starving.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:05.453
It's probably because I'm eating

00:05:05.453 --> 00:05:07.153
so much less calories than usual.

00:05:07.153 --> 00:05:09.583
Getting into the later weeks of keto,

00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:11.083
I was getting hungry.

00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:12.773
That doesn't mean I wasn't satiated,

00:05:12.773 --> 00:05:15.563
I mean eating a lot of
fats, you get full quickly

00:05:15.563 --> 00:05:16.653
and you're no longer hungry.

00:05:16.653 --> 00:05:19.073
But when I say hungry, I
mean more like cravings.

00:05:19.073 --> 00:05:21.596
Bananas, cookies and cream milkshakes,

00:05:22.463 --> 00:05:25.053
and then I even noticed a
pattern where I was hungry,

00:05:25.053 --> 00:05:26.473
just because I was bored.

00:05:26.473 --> 00:05:30.133
I had a high fat meal, I had
some sardines with guacamole.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:33.223
I'm full. But I wanna munch on something,

00:05:33.223 --> 00:05:34.393
I just wanna eat some chips,

00:05:34.393 --> 00:05:37.403
so I've realized that I like to bored eat.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.963
And on keto, you really can't bored eat.

00:05:39.963 --> 00:05:42.233
Unless you just eat nuts all day,

00:05:42.233 --> 00:05:43.533
I don't understand how many almonds

00:05:43.533 --> 00:05:45.233
you can eat in one day before you.

00:05:47.287 --> 00:05:49.193
I think I broke keto.

00:05:49.193 --> 00:05:53.093
I mean not technically, but I had several

00:05:53.093 --> 00:05:56.793
drinks last night that technically
throws you out of keto.

00:05:56.793 --> 00:06:00.032
They were not sugary
drinks, I just had soda

00:06:00.032 --> 00:06:03.323
and alcohol but that does technically

00:06:03.323 --> 00:06:06.764
take you out of ketosis at
least for a short while so

00:06:06.764 --> 00:06:09.483
you probably think I'm a failure.

00:06:09.483 --> 00:06:13.583
Look, we all make mistakes
and two steps forward

00:06:13.583 --> 00:06:16.653
with one step back, is
still one step forward.

00:06:16.653 --> 00:06:18.553
That's something that
I want you to remember

00:06:18.553 --> 00:06:20.413
and take away from my keto journey.

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:23.383
If you mess up, it's not
the end of the world.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.803
It's doesn't mean that you're a failure.

00:06:24.803 --> 00:06:26.193
Yes, I had a few drinks

00:06:26.193 --> 00:06:28.103
and it took me out of
ketosis for a little bit

00:06:28.103 --> 00:06:30.003
because your body actually metabolizes

00:06:30.003 --> 00:06:32.553
the alcohol and uses that
as energy instead of fats.

00:06:32.553 --> 00:06:34.883
But, it's fine. As soon
as I stopped drinking

00:06:34.883 --> 00:06:37.223
the alcohol, the next
day I was probably back

00:06:37.223 --> 00:06:39.543
in ketosis and everything
was back on track.

00:06:39.543 --> 00:06:41.623
So did it slow down my progress?

00:06:41.623 --> 00:06:44.333
Probably somewhat, but it
wasn't the end of the world.

00:06:44.333 --> 00:06:46.853
If I treated it like it
was the end of the world,

00:06:46.853 --> 00:06:48.573
that would hurt my progress because

00:06:48.573 --> 00:06:50.600
that would demotivate me, and cause me

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.383
to order some cookies and cream milkshakes

00:06:53.383 --> 00:06:54.723
and we know we can't do that on keto.

00:06:54.723 --> 00:06:56.643
I had a renewed determination

00:06:56.643 --> 00:06:58.795
to continue and finish my keto journey.

00:06:58.795 --> 00:07:01.378
(upbeat music)

00:07:06.443 --> 00:07:09.973
One month of keto is in the books!

00:07:09.973 --> 00:07:14.031
I made it, I ate 75 percent
of my calories from fat,

00:07:14.031 --> 00:07:17.253
20 percent from protein,
5 percent from carbs.

00:07:17.253 --> 00:07:18.613
I stuck to this bad boy.

00:07:18.613 --> 00:07:21.303
But let's talk summary, let's
talk about what happened.

00:07:21.303 --> 00:07:22.813
First and foremost, body.

00:07:22.813 --> 00:07:26.166
I started this diet at 208 pounds,

00:07:27.217 --> 00:07:29.973
I weighed in this morning at 202 pounds.

00:07:29.973 --> 00:07:32.873
So that's a six pound
weight loss in 4 weeks,

00:07:32.873 --> 00:07:34.653
sounds pretty appropriate, about a pound

00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:35.553
and a half per week.

00:07:35.553 --> 00:07:37.293
My abs are showing a little bit more,

00:07:37.293 --> 00:07:39.323
which gets me really excited for summer.

00:07:39.323 --> 00:07:41.613
Now when it comes to my mind, I don't

00:07:41.613 --> 00:07:46.413
necessarily feel any big
difference that jumps out.

00:07:46.413 --> 00:07:49.123
But I do notice that
I don't crash as much,

00:07:49.123 --> 00:07:50.843
especially in the midday section.

00:07:52.477 --> 00:07:55.060
(upbeat music)

00:08:07.422 --> 00:08:10.384
For the average healthy
person going on a short

00:08:10.384 --> 00:08:13.512
course of keto will help
them lose some weight

00:08:13.512 --> 00:08:15.722
and it probably won't be
detrimental to their health.

00:08:15.722 --> 00:08:18.802
If you're gonna start a new
diet, any diet for that matter,

00:08:18.802 --> 00:08:20.842
go see your doctor and
have that conversation.

00:08:20.842 --> 00:08:23.162
Figure out what are the
benefits versus harms

00:08:23.162 --> 00:08:25.392
so you can make the most educated decision

00:08:25.392 --> 00:08:26.752
possible moving forward.

00:08:26.752 --> 00:08:29.315
I hope you guys enjoyed
me trying out keto,

00:08:30.206 --> 00:08:31.982
if you want me to continue
trying out weird things,

00:08:31.982 --> 00:08:34.342
diets, whatever, drop it
down below in the comments

00:08:34.342 --> 00:08:37.122
and smash that like button
and if you tried keto

00:08:37.122 --> 00:08:39.022
and you had an experience of your own,

00:08:39.022 --> 00:08:40.802
also jump into the comments section

00:08:40.802 --> 00:08:43.005
as you know, I'm very active down there.

00:08:45.552 --> 00:08:48.142
And if you wanna see more
about my take on diets,

00:08:48.142 --> 00:08:50.582
click here for my playlist and as always,

00:08:50.582 --> 00:08:52.901
stay happy and healthy.

00:08:52.901 --> 00:08:56.068
(upbeat techno music)

